{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "03", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "07", "M": "13", "S": "04"}}, "news": [{"title": "Panaji residents seek rejection of five NBCC projects over infrastructure limits", "para": "Residents of Panaji have voiced their concerns over five redevelopment projects by NBCC due to insufficient infrastructure. A letter to Mayor Rohit Monserrate highlights issues with drainage, water supply, and electricity. People for Panaji\u2019s secretary, Chryselle Dias, criticized the government for its apparent double standards regarding development approvals. Citizens urge careful examination of the city\u2019s rainfall deficits and existing infrastructure challenges before proceeding with these projects.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/panaji-residents-seek-rejection-of-five-nbcc-projects-over-infrastructure-limits/134652600?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-123350/134652600.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Uttarakhand GST department recovers \u20b92.25 crore as tax evasion from Eden Senior Living & Wellness", "para": "Following a thorough inspection of Eden Senior Living & Wellness by the Uttarakhand tax department, it became evident that discrepancies in GST payments had occurred. The company responded by depositing Rs 2.25 crore towards its identified tax liability of Rs 12.50 crore, mainly stemming from improper input tax credit usage.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/uttarakhand-gst-department-recovers-2-25-crore-as-tax-evasion-from-eden-senior-living-wellness/134652582?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-103/134652582.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "India retail leasing falls 4.4% to 2.22 million sq ft in Q3 2026: Report", "para": "Retail leasing across India's top eight cities stood at 2.22 million sq ft in Q3 2026, down 7.3% sequentially and 4.4% year-on-year, while Grade A mall vacancy declined to 4.8%. About 12.7 million sq ft of new mall supply is expected through 2028.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/retail/india-retail-leasing-falls-4-4-to-2-22-million-sq-ft-in-q3-2026-report/134651392?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-279148/134651392.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "retail"}]}